```java
http
    .csrf()
    .ignoringAntMatchers("/h2-console/**")
    .disable()
```

The `.disable()` here — `.csrf()` returns `CsrfConfigurer<HttpSecurity>`, `.ignoringAntMatchers(...)` returns CsrfConfigurer, `.disable()` — AbstractConfigurableSecurityBuilder.disable()? CsrfConfigurer extends AbstractHttpConfigurer which extends AbstractConfigurableSecurityBuilder — `.disable()` returns H (HttpSecurity) and disables THE CONFIGURER (csrf). So csrf is disabled entirely. The ignoringAntMatchers is vestigial. So my lambda: `.csrf(csrf -> csrf.disable())` ✓ same semantics.

