7.9.3 effective behavior: unmatched = PUBLIC (FilterSecurityInterceptor null-attributes). If I omit anyRequest with authorizeHttpRequests → unmatched = DENIED. That would 401/403 all static assets not covered by explicit rules (e.g. `/main.js`, `/global.css`, `/favicon.ico`, `/index.html`, `/`!) — breaking e2e. So: `anyRequest().permitAll()` is REQUIRED to preserve 7.9.3 behavior. 

Hmm — wait, actually, let me double-check one thing: in the REAL 7.9.3 app running with Undertow, did visiting `/` really give index.html (200) and not 401? I reasoned FilterSecurityInterceptor → public. But hmm — `httpBasic()` + `.exceptionHandling().authenticationEntryPoint(problemSupport)` — for public requests, no auth required, pass through. The resource handler serves index.html. YES — the JHipster 7.9.3 prod app definitely served the SPA at :8080 without auth (that's how JHipster 7 e2e worked with `ci:e2e:server:start` = plain java -jar at 8080 + cypress baseUrl 8080). CONFIRMED by the e2e setup itself: `ci:e2e:run` runs the packaged jar and cypress against 8080. ✓

So: `anyRequest().permitAll()`. And with @EnableMethodSecurity, method security (@PreAuthorize on services, e.g. UserService @PreAuthorize) still enforces auth on API level via the /api/** rules.

One more consideration: the ORDER of rules. `.authorizeHttpRequests` — first match wins (same as before). I keep the 7.9.3 order exactly: OPTIONS /** → app → i18n → content → swagger-ui → test → h2-console → api/authenticate → register → activate → reset-password init/finish → api/admin/** ADMIN → api/** authenticated → management health/info/prometheus → management/** ADMIN. Then anyRequest().permitAll().

Hmm — one question: `.httpBasic(withDefaults())` — 7.9.3 had `.httpBasic()`. In 6.1.5 the no-arg `httpBasic()` still exists (deprecated in 6.2? not sure — 6.1.5: `httpBasic()` and `httpBasic(Customizer)` both exist). I'll use `.httpBasic(withDefaults())` — clean.

`.apply(securityConfigurerAdapter())` — `apply` is deprecated in 6.1? `HttpSecurity.apply(SecurityConfigurerAdapter)` — deprecated since 5.2?? no... it exists in 6.1 (deprecated in 6.2? removed 7). It compiles in 6.1.5. Alternatively `.with(securityConfigurerAdapter(), withDefaults())`. Hmm — 7.9.3 uses `.apply(securityConfigurerAdapter())`. I'll keep `.apply(...)`. Hmm — but wait, `JWTConfigurer extends AbstractHttpConfigurer` — fine.

Actually — hmm, `AbstractHttpConfigurer` and `apply` — in Spring Security 6.1.5, is `apply` still there? Yes (`deprecated` in 6.2? no — deprecated since 6.2? whatever — it exists in 6.1.5, possibly with deprecation warning; checkstyle doesn't check deprecation).

